1
00:03:59,254 --> 00:04:00,672
Doug?

2
00:04:02,841 --> 00:04:05,342
Honey, are you all right?

3
00:04:07,386 --> 00:04:08,847
You're dreaming.

4
00:04:11,265 --> 00:04:13,225
Was it about Mars?

5
00:04:19,063 --> 00:04:20,732
Is that better?

6
00:04:23,442 --> 00:04:25,110
My poor baby.

7
00:04:26,194 --> 00:04:28,614
This is getting to be
an obsession.

8
00:04:36,787 --> 00:04:38,080
Was she there?

9
00:04:40,125 --> 00:04:41,543
Who?

10
00:04:43,585 --> 00:04:46,422
The one you told me about.
The brunette.

11
00:04:47,631 --> 00:04:48,881
Lori.

12
00:04:51,801 --> 00:04:54,764
I can't believe
you're jealous of a dream.

13
00:04:55,471 --> 00:04:58,349
- Who is she?
- Nobody.

14
00:04:58,433 --> 00:05:00,643
"Nobody"? What's her name?

15
00:05:00,727 --> 00:05:02,143
I don't know.

16
00:05:03,479 --> 00:05:05,230
- Tell me!
- I don't know!

17
00:05:05,314 --> 00:05:07,608
You better tell me!

18
00:05:07,691 --> 00:05:11,444
It's not funny, Doug.
You dream about her every night.

19
00:05:11,527 --> 00:05:14,239
And I'm always back
in the morning.

20
00:05:14,281 --> 00:05:15,740
Let me go!

21
00:05:18,284 --> 00:05:20,411
Come on, baby.

22
00:05:20,453 --> 00:05:23,497
You know you're the girl
of my dreams.

23
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:25,248
You mean it?

24
00:05:26,374 --> 00:05:28,292
You know I do.

25
00:05:37,760 --> 00:05:40,678
I'll give you
something to dream about.

26
00:05:50,647 --> 00:05:50,814
The chairman defended the attack,
saying that space-based weapons...

27
00:05:50,814 --> 00:05:54,398
The chairman defended the attack,
saying that space-based weapons...

28
00:05:54,482 --> 00:05:58,571
are our only defense against the
southern block's numerical superiority.

29
00:05:58,655 --> 00:06:01,072
And more violence
last night on Mars...

30
00:06:01,155 --> 00:06:03,492
where terrorists
demanding independence...

31
00:06:03,534 --> 00:06:06,993
once again halted the extraction
of terbinium ore.

32
00:06:11,958 --> 00:06:14,166
Kuato and his so-called
freedom brigade...

33
00:06:14,250 --> 00:06:16,294
claimed credit
for this latest bombing,

34
00:06:16,336 --> 00:06:19,630
which attempted to reopen
the sealed-off Pyramid Mines.

35
00:06:23,134 --> 00:06:26,595
Mars military restored order
with minimal use of force...

36
00:06:26,679 --> 00:06:30,474
and all damage to the strategic facility
was repaired within hours.

37
00:06:30,516 --> 00:06:32,017
No cameras!

38
00:06:32,101 --> 00:06:36,187
With one mine already closed,
Mars administrator Vilos Cohaagen...

39
00:06:36,271 --> 00:06:38,357
vowed that troops
would be used if necessary...

40
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:42,277
to keep production
at full capacity.

41
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:45,779
No wonder you're having nightmares.
You're always watching the news.

42
00:06:50,075 --> 00:06:52,368
- Lori.
- Doug?

43
00:06:52,410 --> 00:06:55,788
- Let's do it.
- Do what?

44
00:06:55,872 --> 00:06:57,291
Move to Mars.

45
00:06:58,375 --> 00:07:01,794
Why do you have to spoil
a perfectly wonderful morning?

46
00:07:03,463 --> 00:07:04,882
Just think about it.

47
00:07:07,257 --> 00:07:10,636
We've been through this before.
You'd hate it on Mars.

48
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:13,554
It's dry, it's ugly, it's boring.

49
00:07:14,598 --> 00:07:18,725
I mean, really, a revolution
could break out there any second.

50
00:07:18,808 --> 00:07:20,728
Cohaagen says
it's just a few extremists.

51
00:07:21,979 --> 00:07:23,398
You believe him?

52
00:07:29,403 --> 00:07:31,695
Okay. Forget about it.

53
00:07:34,532 --> 00:07:39,077
Absolutely not. Mars was colonized by
the northern block at enormous expense.

54
00:07:39,161 --> 00:07:42,873
Our entire war effort
depends on their terbinium.

55
00:07:42,914 --> 00:07:44,874
It's absurd to think
we'd give it away...

56
00:07:44,915 --> 00:07:47,544
just because some lazy mutants
think they own the planet.

57
00:07:49,212 --> 00:07:52,173
- Maybe we should take a trip.
- Any comment on the rumor...

58
00:07:52,256 --> 00:07:55,176
- Lori, move.
- that you've closed the Pyramid Mine...

59
00:07:55,259 --> 00:07:57,177
because you found
alien artifacts inside?

60
00:07:57,260 --> 00:08:00,263
There's a lot better places
than Mars.

61
00:08:00,305 --> 00:08:03,267
What about Saturn?
Don't you wanna see Saturn?

62
00:08:03,309 --> 00:08:07,312
I wish we could find some artifacts.
Our tourist industry could use a boost.

63
00:08:07,395 --> 00:08:09,939
Everybody says that its gorgeous.

64
00:08:10,022 --> 00:08:13,735
The fact is, it's Mr. Kuato and his
terrorists who spread these rumors...

65
00:08:13,818 --> 00:08:15,904
to undermine trust
in the government.

66
00:08:15,987 --> 00:08:19,615
We could take a long space cruise,
the kind with nothing to do.

67
00:08:19,698 --> 00:08:23,367
- Have you found Kuato yet?
- We don't even know what he looks like.

68
00:08:23,450 --> 00:08:25,578
- What do you say?
- That's the news.

69
00:08:25,620 --> 00:08:27,580
- Stay tuned for weather.
- I'm late.

70
00:08:27,622 --> 00:08:29,208
But first, this.

71
00:08:30,666 --> 00:08:33,586
- Tonight, World Series Game Five...
- Sweetheart.

72
00:08:33,670 --> 00:08:35,088
Iive from Tokyo.

73
00:08:37,506 --> 00:08:41,885
I know it's hard being in a new town,
but let's give it a chance, okay?

74
00:08:43,803 --> 00:08:48,806
Don't you understand? I feel like
I was made for something more than this.

75
00:08:49,683 --> 00:08:53,646
I want to do something with my life,
to be somebody.

76
00:08:53,688 --> 00:08:55,689
You are somebody.

77
00:08:55,772 --> 00:08:57,899
You're the man I love.

78
00:09:02,486 --> 00:09:03,946
Bye.

79
00:09:06,490 --> 00:09:08,408
Have a nice day.

80
00:09:27,218 --> 00:09:30,219
You are now entering
a safety zone.

81
00:09:30,302 --> 00:09:34,682
No unauthorized weapons allowed
beyond this point.

82
00:09:45,067 --> 00:09:48,026
Would you like to ski...

83
00:09:48,110 --> 00:09:50,572
but you're snowed under
with work?

84
00:09:50,613 --> 00:09:54,657
Do you dream of a vacation
at the bottom of the ocean...

85
00:09:54,741 --> 00:09:56,661
but you can't float the bill?

86
00:09:57,537 --> 00:10:00,998
Have you always wanted
to climb the mountains of Mars...

87
00:10:02,541 --> 00:10:04,626
but now you're over the hill?

88
00:10:05,961 --> 00:10:07,879
Then come to Rekall lncorporated...

89
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:11,007
where you can buy the memory
of your ideal vacation...

90
00:10:11,090 --> 00:10:13,717
cheaper, safer and better
than the real thing.

91
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:16,554
So don't let life pass you by.

92
00:10:16,637 --> 00:10:20,223
Call Rekall
for the memory of a lifetime.

93
00:10:20,307 --> 00:10:24,227
For the memory of a lifetime

94
00:10:24,269 --> 00:10:27,688
Rekall, Rekall, Rekall

95
00:10:46,497 --> 00:10:47,581
Harry.

96
00:10:51,002 --> 00:10:53,377
- You ever hear of Rekall?
- Rekall?

97
00:10:53,419 --> 00:10:55,380
Where they sell
those fake memories.

98
00:10:55,464 --> 00:10:56,924
Oh, Rekall.

99
00:10:59,634 --> 00:11:01,720
- Thinking of going there?
- Maybe.

100
00:11:01,804 --> 00:11:03,764
- Well, don't.
- Why not?

101
00:11:03,806 --> 00:11:08,351
A friend of mine tried it,
nearly got himself lobotomized.

102
00:11:09,018 --> 00:11:10,269
No shit?

103
00:11:10,353 --> 00:11:13,105
Don't fuck with your brain.
It ain't worth it.

104
00:11:14,940 --> 00:11:16,858
I guess not.

105
00:12:01,190 --> 00:12:03,607
Good afternoon.
Welcome to Rekall.

106
00:12:03,649 --> 00:12:05,777
Douglas Quaid.
I have an appointment.

107
00:12:09,198 --> 00:12:10,656
- Bob?
- Yeah?

108
00:12:10,739 --> 00:12:13,785
- Doug Quaid is here to see you.
- I'll be right out.

109
00:12:14,870 --> 00:12:16,661
Just one minute, Mr. Quaid.

110
00:12:17,829 --> 00:12:19,290
Thank you.

111
00:12:27,882 --> 00:12:30,466
- Paul McClane. Good to see you.
- Nice to meet you.

112
00:12:30,508 --> 00:12:32,176
Come on in.

113
00:12:33,803 --> 00:12:36,013
- Make yourself comfortable.
- Thank you.

114
00:12:37,097 --> 00:12:38,807
Help me out here, Doug.

115
00:12:38,891 --> 00:12:41,643
- You were interested in a memory of--
- Mars.

116
00:12:42,685 --> 00:12:44,353
Yeah. Mars.

117
00:12:44,437 --> 00:12:45,855
Is there a problem?

118
00:12:47,859 --> 00:12:49,525
To be perfectly honest...

119
00:12:49,609 --> 00:12:51,152
if you like outer space...

120
00:12:51,235 --> 00:12:55,780
you'd be happier with
one of our Saturn cruises.

121
00:12:55,864 --> 00:12:58,700
I'm not interested in Saturn.
I said Mars.

122
00:12:59,534 --> 00:13:01,245
Okay. You're the boss.

123
00:13:02,328 --> 00:13:04,371
Mars it is.

124
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:06,750
Now, let me see.

125
00:13:06,833 --> 00:13:08,875
The basic Mars package...

126
00:13:08,958 --> 00:13:12,297
will run you 899 credits.

127
00:13:12,380 --> 00:13:15,840
Now, that's for two full weeks
of memories, complete in every detail.

128
00:13:15,882 --> 00:13:19,386
A longer trip is more expensive
because it's a deeper implant.

129
00:13:19,470 --> 00:13:21,887
What's in the two-week package?

130
00:13:21,970 --> 00:13:25,516
When you go Rekall, you get nothing
but first-class memories.

131
00:13:26,684 --> 00:13:30,687
Private shuttle cabin, deluxe suite
at the Hilton, all the major sights:

132
00:13:30,771 --> 00:13:33,066
Mount Pyramid,
the Grand Canals...

133
00:13:33,149 --> 00:13:35,651
and, of course, Venusville.

134
00:13:35,734 --> 00:13:37,569
But how real does it seem?

135
00:13:37,611 --> 00:13:41,864
- As real as any memory in your head.
- Don't bullshit me.

136
00:13:41,906 --> 00:13:44,867
I'm telling you, your brain
will not know the difference.

137
00:13:44,951 --> 00:13:46,994
That's guaranteed
or your money back.

138
00:13:47,078 --> 00:13:50,413
What about the guy you lobotomized?
Did he get a refund?

139
00:13:54,042 --> 00:13:56,086
You're talking ancient history.

140
00:13:56,169 --> 00:14:00,174
Nowadays traveling with Rekall
is safer than getting on a rocket.

141
00:14:00,255 --> 00:14:02,174
Check out those statistics.

142
00:14:02,258 --> 00:14:05,929
Besides, a real holiday
is a pain in the butt.

143
00:14:06,012 --> 00:14:08,680
You got lost luggage,
lousy weather...

144
00:14:08,763 --> 00:14:10,723
crooked taxi drivers.

145
00:14:10,807 --> 00:14:13,018
When you travel with Rekall...

146
00:14:13,102 --> 00:14:16,104
everything is perfect.

147
00:14:16,187 --> 00:14:17,273
What do you say?

148
00:14:19,441 --> 00:14:22,275
- All right.
- Smart move.

149
00:14:22,317 --> 00:14:25,655
While you fill out
this questionnaire,

150
00:14:25,738 --> 00:14:28,239
I'll familiarize you
with some of our options.

151
00:14:28,322 --> 00:14:29,783
No options.

152
00:14:30,993 --> 00:14:34,369
Whatever you say.
Let me ask you one question.

153
00:14:35,204 --> 00:14:37,249
What is exactly the same...

154
00:14:37,290 --> 00:14:40,458
about every single vacation
you have ever taken?

155
00:14:41,669 --> 00:14:42,795
I give up.

156
00:14:42,837 --> 00:14:45,631
You. You're the same.

157
00:14:45,671 --> 00:14:48,258
No matter where you go,
it's always you.

158
00:14:49,134 --> 00:14:51,678
Let me suggest
that you take a vacation...

159
00:14:51,761 --> 00:14:53,137
from yourself.

160
00:14:53,220 --> 00:14:54,805
I know, it sounds wild.

161
00:14:54,888 --> 00:14:57,809
It is the latest thing in travel.
We call it the Ego Trip.

162
00:14:58,560 --> 00:15:00,060
I'm not interested.

163
00:15:00,144 --> 00:15:01,937
You're gonna love this, Doug.

164
00:15:01,979 --> 00:15:05,690
We offer you a choice of
alternate identities during your trip.

165
00:15:05,773 --> 00:15:09,319
Why go to Mars as a tourist
when you can go as a playboy...

166
00:15:09,402 --> 00:15:11,280
or a famous jock or--

167
00:15:11,363 --> 00:15:12,446
"Secret agent."

168
00:15:12,529 --> 00:15:14,281
How much is that?

169
00:15:17,368 --> 00:15:19,745
Let me tantalize you.

170
00:15:19,828 --> 00:15:24,623
You are a top operative under deep cover
on your most important mission.

171
00:15:24,665 --> 00:15:27,293
People are trying to kill you.

172
00:15:27,334 --> 00:15:30,630
You meet this beautiful,
exotic woman.

173
00:15:30,672 --> 00:15:31,796
Go on.

174
00:15:31,880 --> 00:15:34,507
I don't wanna spoil it for you...

175
00:15:34,591 --> 00:15:36,802
but by the time
the trip is over...

176
00:15:36,844 --> 00:15:40,848
you get the girl, kill the bad guys
and save the entire planet.

177
00:15:40,931 --> 00:15:42,433
Now, you tell me.

178
00:15:42,516 --> 00:15:45,434
Isn't that worth
a measly 300 credits?

179
00:15:59,864 --> 00:16:01,074
Your first trip?

180
00:16:02,367 --> 00:16:05,328
Don't worry. Things hardly ever
fuck up around here.

181
00:16:06,537 --> 00:16:08,539
Good evening... Doug.

182
00:16:08,623 --> 00:16:10,999
- I'm Dr. Lull.
- Nice to meet you.

183
00:16:11,041 --> 00:16:14,836
Ernie, patch in matrix 62-B-37.

184
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:17,880
Would you like us to integrate
some alien stuff?

185
00:16:17,922 --> 00:16:19,882
Sure. Why not?

186
00:16:21,467 --> 00:16:22,886
Two-headed monsters?

187
00:16:22,969 --> 00:16:24,887
Don't you watch the news?

188
00:16:24,970 --> 00:16:28,517
- We're doing alien artifacts now.
- It's wild.

189
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:31,518
Yeah, they date back
a million years.

190
00:16:32,811 --> 00:16:34,563
- Ernie?
- That's a new one.

191
00:16:34,605 --> 00:16:36,397
- Blue sky on Mars.
- Been married long?

192
00:16:37,481 --> 00:16:39,942
- Eight years.
- Oh, I see.

193
00:16:40,025 --> 00:16:42,527
Slipping away for
a little hanky-panky.

194
00:16:42,610 --> 00:16:45,363
- No. I'm fascinated with Mars.
- All systems go.

195
00:16:45,446 --> 00:16:47,367
Number seven.

196
00:16:47,408 --> 00:16:48,868
Ready for dreamland?

197
00:16:51,452 --> 00:16:55,580
I'll be asking you some questions
so we can fine-tune the Ego program.

198
00:16:55,664 --> 00:16:58,584
You answer honestly,
you'll enjoy yourself much more.

199
00:16:58,668 --> 00:17:01,546
- Your sexual orientation.
- Hetero.

200
00:17:07,008 --> 00:17:09,009
How do you like your women?

201
00:17:09,093 --> 00:17:12,055
Blonde? Brunette? Redhead?

202
00:17:12,889 --> 00:17:14,182
Brunette.

203
00:17:16,434 --> 00:17:20,396
Slim. Athletic. Voluptuous.

204
00:17:23,815 --> 00:17:25,275
Athletic.

205
00:17:29,571 --> 00:17:33,449
Demure. Aggressive. Sleazy.

206
00:17:33,533 --> 00:17:35,075
Be honest.

207
00:17:35,159 --> 00:17:36,577
Sleazy.

208
00:17:40,955 --> 00:17:42,206
Demure.

209
00:17:44,876 --> 00:17:46,295
41A, Ernie.

210
00:17:48,170 --> 00:17:50,255
Boy, is he gonna have
a wild time.

211
00:17:51,299 --> 00:17:54,801
- He's not gonna want to come back.
- That's for sure.

212
00:18:16,030 --> 00:18:17,114
So...

213
00:18:17,198 --> 00:18:19,116
what do you say?

214
00:18:19,158 --> 00:18:22,118
I'm not so sure,
and I don't get a souvenir.

215
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:27,580
Not true. We supply T-shirts,
snapshots of you at the site...

216
00:18:27,664 --> 00:18:29,583
and even letters from--

217
00:18:32,918 --> 00:18:35,130
- What is it?
- Get down here.

218
00:18:35,214 --> 00:18:37,508
I am with
a very important client.

219
00:18:37,591 --> 00:18:40,009
Looks like we got
another schizoid embolism.

220
00:18:41,719 --> 00:18:43,346
I'll be right back.

221
00:18:43,429 --> 00:18:44,514
Mr. McClane?

222
00:18:46,306 --> 00:18:48,016
Bob! What's wrong?

223
00:18:48,099 --> 00:18:50,018
Don't let her leave!

224
00:18:54,730 --> 00:18:56,525
Get off!

225
00:18:58,402 --> 00:19:00,152
You blew my cover!

226
00:19:00,236 --> 00:19:03,448
You can't do a simple
goddamn double implant?

227
00:19:03,532 --> 00:19:05,198
We hit a memory cap.

228
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:07,575
They're coming!
They'll kill you all!

229
00:19:07,659 --> 00:19:10,371
- What is he talking about?
- Let me go!

230
00:19:10,454 --> 00:19:12,371
Mr. Quaid, try to calm down!

231
00:19:14,873 --> 00:19:16,793
My name is not Quaid.

232
00:19:16,876 --> 00:19:20,712
- Let me go! Untie me now!
- Ernie, grab his leg!

233
00:19:20,796 --> 00:19:23,299
- Hold him down!
- Let me go!

234
00:19:47,028 --> 00:19:49,281
Are you all right?

235
00:19:49,364 --> 00:19:52,491
Listen to me.
He's been going on and on about Mars.

236
00:19:52,575 --> 00:19:55,494
- He has really been there.
- Use your head.

237
00:19:55,578 --> 00:19:58,871
He's just acting out the "secret agent"
portion of his ego trip.

238
00:19:58,913 --> 00:20:00,874
- That's not possible.
- Why not?

239
00:20:00,916 --> 00:20:02,751
We haven't implanted it yet.

240
00:20:06,963 --> 00:20:08,214
Oh, shit.

241
00:20:09,842 --> 00:20:13,427
I've been trying to tell you,
someone has erased his memory.

242
00:20:13,510 --> 00:20:14,761
Excuse me.

243
00:20:14,845 --> 00:20:16,595
"Someone"?

244
00:20:16,679 --> 00:20:18,597
We're talking about the Agency.

245
00:20:18,681 --> 00:20:21,393
- Shut up!
- Bob, the client's gone.

246
00:20:23,853 --> 00:20:27,441
Renata, cover up any memory he's got
of us or Rekall.

247
00:20:27,524 --> 00:20:29,733
I'll try.
It's pretty messy in there.

248
00:20:29,816 --> 00:20:33,070
Ernie, dump him in a cab.
Tiffany, you help him.

249
00:20:33,112 --> 00:20:36,113
I'm gonna destroy his file
and refund his money.

250
00:20:36,196 --> 00:20:39,534
And if anybody comes asking,
we never heard of Douglas Quaid.

251
00:20:53,964 --> 00:20:55,382
Where am l?

252
00:20:57,717 --> 00:20:59,636
You're in a Johnnycab.

253
00:20:59,719 --> 00:21:01,304
What am I doing here?

254
