00:49:02,532 --> 00:49:03,993
No, sir.

504
00:49:05,828 --> 00:49:09,288
Because I've got the greatest job
in the solar system.

505
00:49:09,371 --> 00:49:13,460
As long as the terbinium keeps flowing,
I can do anything I want.

506
00:49:13,544 --> 00:49:15,004
Anything.

507
00:49:16,421 --> 00:49:18,131
In fact...

508
00:49:18,172 --> 00:49:21,467
my only worry
is that one day...

509
00:49:21,510 --> 00:49:23,802
if the rebels win...

510
00:49:23,844 --> 00:49:26,430
it all might end...

511
00:49:26,513 --> 00:49:28,099
and you're making it happen!

512
00:49:29,015 --> 00:49:32,018
First you try to kill Quaid,
then he escapes.

513
00:49:32,059 --> 00:49:34,355
He had help from our side, sir.

514
00:49:35,563 --> 00:49:36,772
I know that.

515
00:49:38,858 --> 00:49:41,195
- But I thought--
- Who told you to think?

516
00:49:41,236 --> 00:49:44,321
I don't give you enough information
to think.

517
00:49:45,865 --> 00:49:49,533
You do what you're told.
That's what you do.

518
00:49:51,703 --> 00:49:52,996
Yes, sir.

519
00:49:58,376 --> 00:49:59,961
Let's get to business.

520
00:50:01,669 --> 00:50:04,048
We've got
a tricky situation here.

521
00:50:04,089 --> 00:50:06,467
Kuato wants
what's in Quaid's head.

522
00:50:07,799 --> 00:50:11,137
He might be able to get it.
They say he's psychic.

523
00:50:12,555 --> 00:50:15,474
I have a plan
to keep this from happening.

524
00:50:18,895 --> 00:50:20,853
Suppose you could play along?

525
00:50:20,895 --> 00:50:23,023
- Yes, sir.
- Great.

526
00:50:23,106 --> 00:50:25,567
Otherwise, I'll erase your ass.

527
00:50:43,708 --> 00:50:47,836
You need a taxi?
I got magazines, music, whisky.

528
00:50:47,920 --> 00:50:50,339
You need a cab?
Come on!

529
00:51:15,946 --> 00:51:17,406
Can I help you?

530
00:51:17,447 --> 00:51:20,031
I would like a room, please.

531
00:51:25,122 --> 00:51:28,082
Nice to have you back, Mr. Brubaker.
Would you like the same suite?

532
00:51:28,165 --> 00:51:29,542
Definitely.

533
00:51:31,792 --> 00:51:33,878
You've left something in our safe.

534
00:51:33,962 --> 00:51:34,879
Could you get it?

535
00:51:41,176 --> 00:51:42,761
Identification?

536
00:51:52,103 --> 00:51:54,522
- I'll encode your room key.
- Thank you.

537
00:52:10,995 --> 00:52:14,290
- Suite 610 in the east wing.
- Thank you.

538
00:52:14,331 --> 00:52:16,835
- Could I borrow your pen, please?
- Certainly.

539
00:52:28,888 --> 00:52:30,137
Thank you.

540
00:52:35,352 --> 00:52:37,852
Hey, man, you need a cab?

541
00:52:37,935 --> 00:52:42,399
- What's wrong with this one?
- He ain't got five kids to feed.

542
00:52:42,483 --> 00:52:44,901
- Where's yours?
- Right over there.

543
00:52:47,236 --> 00:52:49,988
Hey, asshole!
That's my fare!

544
00:52:50,072 --> 00:52:51,449
Eat this!

545
00:52:51,532 --> 00:52:52,867
Damn you, Benny!

546
00:52:59,039 --> 00:53:00,665
Welcome to Mars, man!

547
00:53:04,877 --> 00:53:08,465
- What was that, an accident?
- That's the rebels.

548
00:53:08,548 --> 00:53:10,006
Let's get outta here...

549
00:53:10,049 --> 00:53:11,967
before they arrest us!

550
00:53:12,051 --> 00:53:14,304
What do the rebels want?

551
00:53:14,346 --> 00:53:17,347
The usual.
More money, more freedom, more air.

552
00:53:22,393 --> 00:53:23,685
So, where to?

553
00:53:23,769 --> 00:53:25,562
Last Resort.

554
00:53:25,604 --> 00:53:27,649
You're getting off
to an early start.

555
00:53:28,564 --> 00:53:30,817
- First time on Mars?
- Yes.

556
00:53:30,900 --> 00:53:32,737
Well, actually, no.

557
00:53:32,821 --> 00:53:34,572
Well, sort of.

558
00:53:34,656 --> 00:53:38,659
The man don't even know
whether he's been to Mars or not.

559
00:53:49,041 --> 00:53:51,461
Voila. Venusville.

560
00:53:52,754 --> 00:53:55,047
Hey, you see anything you like?

561
00:53:59,094 --> 00:54:02,429
End of the line.
We'd better walk from here.

562
00:54:02,471 --> 00:54:04,390
I'll show you where.

563
00:54:04,473 --> 00:54:08,226
- Do you want to know the future?
- What about the past?

564
00:54:08,309 --> 00:54:12,063
It's around the corner,
right down this alley.

565
00:54:12,105 --> 00:54:14,064
They got everything.

566
00:54:16,609 --> 00:54:18,570
Not bad, huh?

567
00:54:20,030 --> 00:54:23,907
Read your palm? Your mind? Your aura?
Probe the secrets of your heart?

568
00:54:24,658 --> 00:54:26,744
I bet I can guess
your birthday.

569
00:54:26,827 --> 00:54:29,787
- You're a Taurus, right?
- How did you guess?

570
00:54:32,458 --> 00:54:34,749
- Tell me, are all psychics--
- Freaks?

571
00:54:34,833 --> 00:54:36,878
Afraid so.
It goes with the territory.

572
00:54:36,961 --> 00:54:42,132
- What happened to them?
- Cheap domes, no air to clean the rays.

573
00:54:42,215 --> 00:54:46,220
This is it. The Last Resort.
You sure you want to go in here?

574
00:54:46,302 --> 00:54:49,431
- Why not?
- There's a better place down there.

575
00:54:49,514 --> 00:54:52,476
The girls are cleaner,
the liquor ain't watered down--

576
00:54:52,517 --> 00:54:54,767
Sure, and you get kickbacks.

577
00:54:54,851 --> 00:54:57,771
Hey, man,
I got five kids to feed.

578
00:54:57,855 --> 00:54:59,772
Take them to the dentist.

579
00:54:59,814 --> 00:55:02,318
Thanks, mister!
I'll be waiting for you.

580
00:55:02,401 --> 00:55:04,778
Take your time.
Benny's the name.

581
00:55:24,671 --> 00:55:26,756
- What do you want?
- Melina.

582
00:55:26,839 --> 00:55:28,591
She's busy.

583
00:55:28,674 --> 00:55:30,760
But Mary here, she's free.

584
00:55:30,801 --> 00:55:34,262
Well, not free, honey, but...

585
00:55:34,971 --> 00:55:36,181
available.

586
00:55:39,350 --> 00:55:41,686
Thanks.
I'll wait for Melina.

587
00:55:41,770 --> 00:55:43,022
Earth slime.

588
00:55:43,064 --> 00:55:45,773
Thing is, friend,
Mel's real picky.

589
00:55:45,856 --> 00:55:47,983
She sticks to her regulars.

590
00:55:48,067 --> 00:55:50,028
She'll like me.

591
00:55:51,154 --> 00:55:52,529
Mel!

592
00:56:30,229 --> 00:56:31,523
Hello, Hauser.

593
00:56:32,566 --> 00:56:34,526
Still bulging, I see.

594
00:56:35,986 --> 00:56:39,238
- What you been feeding this thing?
- Blondes.

595
00:56:41,198 --> 00:56:43,116
I think it's still hungry.

596
00:56:45,493 --> 00:56:48,539
You got a lot of nerve
showing your face around here, Hauser.

597
00:56:48,623 --> 00:56:50,665
Look who's talking.

598
00:56:50,748 --> 00:56:53,543
Hey, Tony,
give the big guy a break.

599
00:56:53,626 --> 00:56:55,963
Relax. You'll live longer.

600
00:56:56,046 --> 00:56:57,462
Come on.

601
00:57:03,092 --> 00:57:06,722
- Honey, take care of Tony, will you?
- No problem.

602
00:57:06,805 --> 00:57:09,765
If you need any help with this one,
give me a holler.

603
00:57:24,613 --> 00:57:26,698
You son of a bitch.

604
00:57:26,740 --> 00:57:29,365
You're alive? I thought that
Cohaagen tortured you to death.

605
00:57:29,449 --> 00:57:31,286
Well, I guess he didn't.

606
00:57:31,369 --> 00:57:35,204
And you couldn't get me a message? You
never wondered what happened to me?

607
00:57:42,795 --> 00:57:45,089
Hauser, thank God you're alive.

608
00:57:46,215 --> 00:57:48,550
Melin-- Melina.
Melina.

609
00:57:50,552 --> 00:57:53,431
- I have to tell you something.
- What?

610
00:57:53,473 --> 00:57:57,100
- I don't remember you.
- What are you talking about?

611
00:57:57,184 --> 00:57:59,311
I don't remember you.

612
00:57:59,394 --> 00:58:02,855
I don't remember us.
I don't even remember me.

613
00:58:04,940 --> 00:58:07,361
Did you get amnesia?
How did you get here?

614
00:58:07,442 --> 00:58:09,819
- Hauser left me a note.
- You're Hauser.

615
00:58:09,903 --> 00:58:11,821
Not anymore.

616
00:58:11,905 --> 00:58:15,033
Now I'm Quaid.
Douglas Quaid.

617
00:58:18,204 --> 00:58:22,247
- Hauser, you've lost your mind.
- No, Cohaagen stole it.

618
00:58:22,331 --> 00:58:26,918
He found out that Hauser switched sides,
so he turned him into somebody else: me.

619
00:58:27,001 --> 00:58:28,419
This is too weird.

620
00:58:28,503 --> 00:58:31,131
He dumped me on earth
with a wife and a lousy job--

621
00:58:31,173 --> 00:58:34,132
Did you say wife?
Are you fucking married?

622
00:58:34,174 --> 00:58:36,178
- She wasn't really my wife.
- Oh, she isn't?

623
00:58:36,261 --> 00:58:38,889
How stupid of me.
She was Hauser's wife?

624
00:58:38,972 --> 00:58:41,681
- Forget that I said wife.
- Let's just forget everything.

625
00:58:41,723 --> 00:58:45,520
- I'm sick of hearing your goddamn lies.
- Why would I lie to you?

626
00:58:46,519 --> 00:58:49,940
Because you're still
working for Cohaagen.

627
00:58:49,981 --> 00:58:52,609
Don't be ridiculous.

628
00:58:55,194 --> 00:58:57,447
You never loved me, Hauser.

629
00:58:57,531 --> 00:58:59,489
You just used me to get inside.

630
00:58:59,572 --> 00:59:01,492
Inside what?

631
00:59:05,621 --> 00:59:07,664
I think you'd better leave.

632
00:59:07,747 --> 00:59:11,000
- Melina, Hauser sent me to do something.
- I'm not falling for it.

633
00:59:11,084 --> 00:59:13,252
He says there's enough in here
to nail Cohaagen for good.

634
00:59:13,335 --> 00:59:15,254
- Get out!
- You've got to help me remember!

635
00:59:15,337 --> 00:59:17,464
- I said, get out!
- Melina, please!

636
00:59:17,548 --> 00:59:19,466
People are trying to kill me.

637
00:59:20,342 --> 00:59:22,010
Really?

638
00:59:24,347 --> 00:59:26,431
All right, I'm leaving.

639
00:59:38,441 --> 00:59:41,403
Baby, you make me wish
I had three hands.

640
00:59:41,446 --> 00:59:44,198
I think you're doing
just fine with two.

641
00:59:44,240 --> 00:59:46,657
Excuse me, baby.
We'll pick this up later.

642
00:59:46,741 --> 00:59:49,161
Hey, that didn't take long.

643
00:59:49,244 --> 00:59:51,828
Let me ask you a question.
Did you ever fuck a mutant?

644
00:59:51,911 --> 00:59:54,373
- Take me to the hotel.
- I know these Siamese twins.

645
00:59:54,415 --> 00:59:57,042
Man, you won't know
if you're coming or going.

646
01:00:06,801 --> 01:00:06,843
This afternoon at 4:30 p.m., I signed
an order declaring martial law...

647
01:00:06,843 --> 01:00:10,555
This afternoon at 4:30 p.m., I signed
an order declaring martial law...

648
01:00:10,638 --> 01:00:12,973
throughout the Mars federal colony.

649
01:00:13,056 --> 01:00:17,643
I will not tolerate any further damage
to our mineral export operations.

650
01:00:17,727 --> 01:00:19,896
Mr. Kuato and his terrorists
must understand...

651
01:00:19,979 --> 01:00:23,443
that their self-defeating efforts
will only bring misery and suffering--

652
01:00:27,028 --> 01:00:28,279
Mr. Quaid?

653
01:00:29,030 --> 01:00:30,280
What?

654
01:00:30,363 --> 01:00:32,699
I need to talk to you
about Mr. Hauser.

655
01:00:33,909 --> 01:00:36,245
- Who are you?
- Dr. Edgemar from Rekall.

656
01:00:36,287 --> 01:00:38,621
- How did you find me?
- It's difficult to explain.

657
01:00:38,704 --> 01:00:41,583
Could you open the door?
I'm unarmed.

658
01:00:43,291 --> 01:00:46,295
Don't worry. I'm alone.
May I come in?

659
01:00:48,298 --> 01:00:51,633
- What do you want?
- This will be hard for you to accept.

660
01:00:51,716 --> 01:00:55,221
- I'm listening.
- You're not really standing here now.

661
01:00:56,887 --> 01:01:00,099
- Doc, you could have fooled me.
- I'm quite serious.

662
01:01:00,141 --> 01:01:03,476
You're not here
and neither am l.

663
01:01:03,559 --> 01:01:04,811
That's amazing.

664
01:01:04,895 --> 01:01:07,982
- Where are we?
- At Rekall.

665
01:01:08,066 --> 01:01:09,982
You're strapped into
an implant chair...

666
01:01:10,066 --> 01:01:12,986
and I'm monitoring you
from the psychoprobe console.

667
01:01:14,029 --> 01:01:16,613
Ah, I get it.
I'm dreaming.

668
01:01:16,655 --> 01:01:20,034
And all this is part of the delightful
vacation your company has sold me.

669
01:01:20,117 --> 01:01:21,536
Not exactly.

670
01:01:21,619 --> 01:01:25,747
What you're experiencing is a free-form
delusion based on our memory tapes...

671
01:01:25,830 --> 01:01:28,417
but you're inventing it
yourself as you go along.

672
01:01:29,793 --> 01:01:33,296
If it is my delusion,
who the hell invited you?

673
01:01:33,338 --> 01:01:37,299
I've been artificially implanted
as an emergency measure.

674
01:01:37,341 --> 01:01:40,679
I'm sorry to tell you this,
but you've suffered a schizoid embolism.

675
01:01:40,762 --> 01:01:43,137
We can't snap you
out of your fantasy...

676
01:01:43,179 --> 01:01:46,266
and I've been sent in
to try to talk you down.

677
01:01:46,349 --> 01:01:48,267
How much is Cohaagen
paying you for this?

678
01:01:49,727 --> 01:01:53,857
Think about it. Your dream started
in the middle of the implant procedure.

679
01:01:53,941 --> 01:01:56,358
Everything after that--
the chases, the trip to Mars...

680
01:01:56,441 --> 01:02:00,947
the suite at the Hilton-- are elements
of your Rekall Holiday and Ego Trip.

681
01:02:01,028 --> 01:02:03,447
You paid to be a secret agent.

682
01:02:03,531 --> 01:02:05,993
Bullshit. It's coincidence.

683
01:02:06,076 --> 01:02:08,660
And what about the girl?

684
01:02:08,702 --> 01:02:11,498
Brunette, athletic,
sleazy and demure?

685
01:02:11,582 --> 01:02:14,124
Just as you specified.
Is that coincidence?

686
01:02:14,207 --> 01:02:17,837
She's real. I dreamt about her
before I even went to Rekall.

687
01:02:17,878 --> 01:02:19,964
Mr. Quaid.

688
01:02:20,047 --> 01:02:24,092
Can you hear yourself?
She's real because you dreamed her?

689
01:02:24,175 --> 01:02:27,176
- That's right.
- Maybe this will convince you.

690
01:02:27,260 --> 01:02:29,722
Would you mind opening the door?

691
01:02:31,682 --> 01:02:34,058
- You open it.
- No need to be rude.

692
01:02:34,142 --> 01:02:35,978
I'll do it.

693
01:02:42,567 --> 01:02:43,818
Sweetheart?

694
01:02:46,405 --> 01:02:48,447
Come in, Mrs. Quaid.

695
01:02:52,619 --> 01:02:55,579
- I suppose you're not here either.
- I'm here...

696
01:02:55,662 --> 01:02:58,333
at Rekall.

697
01:03:02,084 --> 01:03:03,753
I love you.

698
01:03:03,836 --> 01:03:07,213
Right. That's why
you tried to kill me.

699
01:03:07,255 --> 01:03:11,302
No. I'd never do
anything to hurt you.

700
01:03:11,385 --> 01:03:13,719
I want you to come back to me.

701
01:03:15,847 --> 01:03:19,099
- Bullshit.
- What's bullshit, Mr. Quaid?

702
01:03:19,183 --> 01:03:23,772
That you're having a paranoid episode
triggered by acute neurochemical trauma?

703
01:03:23,855 --> 01:03:27,815
Or that you're really
an invincible secret agent from Mars...

704
01:03:27,899 --> 01:03:32,110
who's the victim of an interplanetary
conspiracy to make him think...

705
01:03:32,194 --> 01:03:34,155
he's a lowly construction worker?

706
01:03:41,746 --> 01:03:44,082
Stop punishing yourself, Doug.

707
01:03:44,123 --> 01:03:47,084
You're a fine, upstanding man.
You have a beautiful wife who loves you.

708
01:03:48,627 --> 01:03:50,587
Your whole life is ahead of you.

709
01:03:52,546 --> 01:03:55,216
But you've got to want
to return to reality.

710
01:03:57,468 --> 01:04:00,221
Let's assume I do.
Then what?

711
01:04:03,057 --> 01:04:06,142
- Swallow this.
- What is it?

712
01:04:06,226 --> 01:04:10,064
It's a symbol of your desire
to return to reality.

713
01:04:10,147 --> 01:04:12,564
Inside your dream,
you'll fall asleep.

714
01:04:16,486 --> 01:04:20,698
All right, let's say you're telling
the truth and this is all a dream.

715
01:04:20,781 --> 01:04:23,451
Then I could pull this trigger
and it won't matter.

716
01:04:23,535 --> 01:04:26,619
- Doug, don't.
- It won't make a difference to me.

717
01:04:26,661 --> 01:04:31,164
But the consequences to you would be
devastating. In your mind I'll be dead.

718
01:04:31,248 --> 01:04:34,669
With no one to guide you out,
you'll be stuck in permanent psychosis.

719
01:04:34,711 --> 01:04:36,961
Doug, let Dr. Edgemar help you.

720
01:04:37,044 --> 01:04:39,506
The walls of reality
will come crashing down.

721
01:04:39,548 --> 01:04:43,010
One minute you'll be the savior of
the rebel cause, and right after that...

722
01:04:43,094 --> 01:04:45,261
you'll be Cohaagen's bosom buddy.

723
01:04:45,344 --> 01:04:49,266
You'll even have fantasies about
alien civilizations, as you requested...

724
01:04:49,349 --> 01:04:52,059
but in the end,
back on earth you'll be lobotomized!

725
01:04:54,603 --> 01:04:58,064
So get a grip on yourself, Doug,
and put down that gun!

726
01:05:04,029 --> 01:05:07,282
Good. Now take the pill
and put it in your mouth.

727
01:05:12,035 --> 01:05:14,204
Swallow it!

728
01:05:16,664 --> 01:05:19,208
Go ahead, sweetheart.

729
01:05:41,895 --> 01:05:45,232
Now you've done it.
Now you've done it!

730
01:06:06,084 --> 01:06:08,543
That's for making me come to Mars.

731
01:06:09,838 --> 01:06:12,758
You know how much I hate
this fucking planet!

732
01:06:15,176 --> 01:06:16,427
Cuff him.

733
01:06:23,058 --> 01:06:26,436
- I got him.
- Bring him down in the service elevator.

734
01:06:28,729 --> 01:06:30,147
Let's go.

735
01:07:43,548 --> 01:07:44,717
Fuck you!

736
01:07:55,600 --> 01:07:56,518
Doug.

737
01:07:58,436 --> 01:08:00,521
Honey...

738
01:08:00,605 --> 01:08:03,191
you wouldn't hurt me,
would you, sweetheart?

739
01:08:04,941 --> 01:08:08,237
Sweetheart, be reasonable.

740
01:08:08,321 --> 01:08:10,406
After all, we're married.

741
01:08:15,994 --> 01:08:17,410
Consider that a divorce.

742
01:08:19,872 --> 01:08:21,583
That was your wife?

743
01:08:25,501 --> 01:08:26,921
What a bitch.

744
01:08:35,053 --> 01:08:37,136
Hey, get out of the way!

745
01:08:39,598 --> 01:08:42,185
I thought you didn't like me.

746
01:08:42,227 --> 01:08:45,187
If Cohaagen wants you dead,
you might be okay.

747
01:08:45,229 --> 01:08:48,565
- Got it.
- So you've come back to apologize.

748
01:08:48,649 --> 01:08:50,691
Kuato wants to see you.

749
01:08:52,443 --> 01:08:53,903
Come on.

750
01:09:22,344 --> 01:09:23,930
- Now what?
- Jump!

751
01:09:53,624 --> 01:09:57,460
No! Don't do it!
You'll crack the fucking dome!

752
01:10:01,006 --> 01:10:04,300
What are you trying to do, kill us?
The dome will crack!

753
01:10:16,394 --> 01:10:17,478
Move!

754
01:10:19,565 --> 01:10:21,398
Taxi!

755
01:10:22,399 --> 01:10:24,318
Melina! Melina!

756
01:10:27,445 --> 01:10:29,031
- Need a ride?
- Last Resort.

757
01:10:29,114 --> 01:10:30,615
You guys are going in circles.

758
01:10:35,661 --> 01:10:36,662
Jesus!

759
01:10:36,746 --> 01:10:38,957
Come on! You drive!

760
01:10:39,041 --> 01:10:40,165
You guys are in trouble?

761
01:10:40,248 --> 01:10:41,833
Go! Go!

762
01:10:52,762 --> 01:10:55,680
- What are you trying to do to me?
- Shut up and drive!

763
01:10:55,764 --> 01:10:58,016
Hey, I got five kids to feed!

764
01:11:32,045 --> 01:11:33,214
Shit!

765
01:11:33,297 --> 01:11:35,132
No brakes!

766
01:11:35,216 --> 01:11:36,843
You idiot!

767
01:11:40,053 --> 01:11:41,054
What are you doing?

768
01:11:53,564 --> 01:11:56,653
Christ! Now they're after me!

769
01:11:57,654 --> 01:11:59,278
Give me that!

770
01:11:59,362 --> 01:12:01,115
Get out of the way!

771
01:12:07,912 --> 01:12:09,163
Tony!

772
01:12:12,874 --> 01:12:15,252
Get out of the way!
Come on!

773
01:12:15,335 --> 01:12:17,837
Come on! Come on!

774
01:12:21,133 --> 01:12:22,592
Thank you, Tony.

775
01:12:47,531 --> 01:12:49,701
You wanna have some fun?

776
01:12:49,784 --> 01:12:50,950
Where are they?

777
01:12:51,033 --> 01:12:53,744
What are you talking about?
I don't know.

778
01:13:02,337 --> 01:13:03,587
Maybe you know.

779
01:13:10,467 --> 01:13:12,137
Kill them all!

780
01:13:26,317 --> 01:13:27,401
Thumbelina!

781
01:13:52,548 --> 01:13:54,134
Richter!

782
01:13:54,176 --> 01:13:57,385
- A call from Cohaagen!
- Richter here.

783
01:13:57,469 --> 01:14:00,473
- We've got them pinned down.
- Stop fighting and pull out.

784
01:14:00,514 --> 01:14:02,431
But they've got Quaid.
They're protecting him.

785
01:14:03,849 --> 01:14:06,854
Perfect.
Get out of Sector G now.

786
01:14:06,938 --> 01:14:08,479
Don't think.

787
01:14:08,562 --> 01:14:11,315
- Do it!
- Yes, sir.

788
01:14:11,398 --> 01:14:13,068
Pull 'em out.

789
01:14:13,151 --> 01:14:15,485
Everybody, pull out!

790
01:14:15,568 --> 01:14:17,153
Move!

791
01:14:26,205 --> 01:14:29,122
- Cohaagen's sealing off the area!
- Come on, Benny!

792
01:15:30,762 --> 01:15:32,680
The first settlers
are buried here.

793
01:15:32,763 --> 01:15:36,727
They worked themselves to death, but
Cohaagen ended up with all the money.

794
01:15:36,768 --> 01:15:39,603
He built cheap domes and watched
the kids turn into freaks.

795
01:15:39,686 --> 01:15:40,937
I saw them.

796
01:15:41,021 --> 01:15:43,733
And if you want to breathe,
you have to buy his air.

797
01:15:43,816 --> 01:15:45,399
Maybe you can change all that.

798
01:15:45,482 --> 01:15:49,738
Hey, I think my grandpa
might be here.

799
01:15:49,779 --> 01:15:51,406
So what can I do?

800
01:15:51,488 --> 01:15:54,117
Kuato's gonna make you remember some
things you knew when you were Hauser.

801
01:15:54,200 --> 01:15:56,953
- Like what?
- All sorts of things.

802
01:15:57,037 --> 01:16:00,039
- Maybe you'll remember you loved me.
- I don't need Kuato for that.

803
01:16:01,290 --> 01:16:03,292
Since when?

804
01:16:13,133 --> 01:16:14,092
Freeze!

805
01:16:14,134 --> 01:16:16,387
Come on, Melina.

806
01:16:17,721 --> 01:16:19,139
Kuato's waiting.

807
01:16:19,222 --> 01:16:21,475
I didn't find Grandpa, but--

808
01:16:22,809 --> 01:16:24,268
Oh, shit.

809
01:16:24,310 --> 01:16:27,480
- Who's this?
- He helped us get away.

810
01:16:27,563 --> 01:16:31,775
Hey, don't worry about me, man.
I'm on your side.

811
01:16:42,370 --> 01:16:44,328
You're a mutant, huh?

812
01:16:44,370 --> 01:16:46,705
All right, let's go.

813
01:17:01,679 --> 01:17:04,639
- Have you tried ramming down the door?
- You wait here. Follow me.

814
01:17:04,722 --> 01:17:06,641
It won't do any good.

815
01:17:06,724 --> 01:17:10,059
- Cohaagen depressurized the tunnels.
- Then drill through to Section M.

816
01:17:10,142 --> 01:17:13,105
We can't.
We're running out of air.

817
01:17:13,188 --> 01:17:15,190
We need help.

818
01:17:15,273 --> 01:17:17,942
Sit tight.
Melina just got here with Quaid.

819
01:17:19,026 --> 01:17:20,779
I hope he was worth it.

820
01:17:20,862 --> 01:17:22,487
So do l.

821
01:17:24,865 --> 01:17:26,784
- I'm glad you made it.
- You don't look glad.

822
01:17:26,826 --> 01:17:30,120
Cohaagen sealed up Venusville.
He shut off the air.

823
01:17:30,203 --> 01:17:32,455
You must know something
pretty important, Quaid.

824
01:17:32,539 --> 01:17:34,500
He wants you.

825
01:17:34,542 --> 01:17:38,377
If we don't hand you over, everybody
in this sector will be dead by morning.

826
01:17:38,460 --> 01:17:40,129
Then we don't have much choice.

827
01:17:40,212 --> 01:17:41,757
We can't turn him in.

828
01:17:42,881 --> 01:17:45,426
That's up to Kuato.
Come with me, Quaid.

829
01:17:59,605 --> 01:18:01,647
Sit down.

830
01:18:01,730 --> 01:18:04,527
- Where's Kuato?
- On his way.

831
01:18:04,610 --> 01:18:07,155
You heard the rumors
about the Pyramid Mine?

832
01:18:07,238 --> 01:18:09,071
Yeah.

833
01:18:09,155 --> 01:18:12,534
Cohaagen found something weird inside
and it's got him scared shitless.

834
01:18:12,576 --> 01:18:14,868
What? Aliens?

835
01:18:16,245 --> 01:18:19,248
- You tell me.
- I don't know.

836
01:18:19,331 --> 01:18:21,874
Yes, you do.
That's why we brought you here.

837
01:18:21,957 --> 01:18:24,587
Cohaagen's big secret
is buried in that black hole...

838
01:18:24,670 --> 01:18:26,589
you call a brain.

839
01:18:29,215 --> 01:18:31,217
And Kuato's gonna dig it out.

840
01:18:31,259 --> 01:18:34,720
- You're Kuato, right?
- Wrong.

841
01:18:34,762 --> 01:18:38,599
Kuato's a mutant,
so don't get upset when you see him.

842
01:19:17,301 --> 01:19:19,468
What do you want, Mr. Quaid?

843
01:19:20,344 --> 01:19:22,305
Same as you: to remember.

844
01:19:22,347 --> 01:19:25,099
But why?

845
01:19:25,141 --> 01:19:28,435
- To be myself again.
- You are what you do.

846
01:19:31,856 --> 01:19:34,066
A man is defined by his actions...

847
01:19:35,150 --> 01:19:37,277
not his memory.

848
01:19:38,487 --> 01:19:39,779
Please...

849
01:19:39,820 --> 01:19:41,906
take my hands.

850
01:19:47,452 --> 01:19:49,871
Now open your mind to me.

851
01:19:50,832 --> 01:19:52,290
Please.

852
01:19:55,001 --> 01:19:57,630
Open your mind.

853
01:19:59,880 --> 01:20:02,424
Open your mind.

854
01:20:04,511 --> 01:20:07,971
Open your mind.

855
01:20:09,723 --> 01:20:13,434
Open your mind.

856
01:20:15,228 --> 01:20:19,606
Open your mind.

857
01:20:50,174 --> 01:20:52,553
We should blow the thing up
before the rebels turn it on.

858
01:20:52,636 --> 01:20:55,264
I say we throw the switch
and see what happens.

859
01:20:55,348 --> 01:20:57,349
- Don't be an idiot.
- We can't risk it.

860
01:20:57,433 --> 01:21:00,144
The chain reaction could spread
to all the terbinium in the planet.

861
01:21:00,185 --> 01:21:03,396
That means a meltdown,
a meltdown on a planetary scale.

862
01:21:03,479 --> 01:21:05,773
Don't you think whoever
built this thing thought of that?

863
01:21:05,857 --> 01:21:09,028
Who knows what the hell they thought?
They weren't human.

864
01:21:09,111 --> 01:21:11,778
Maybe it's a trap.
Maybe they want a meltdown.

865
01:21:11,862 --> 01:21:14,031
We don't even know
if this piece of junk will work.

866
01:21:14,114 --> 01:21:16,449
What is it?
A million? Half a million?

867
01:21:16,532 --> 01:21:19,828
- About half a million.
- Half a million years old.

868
01:21:19,912 --> 01:21:21,664
Let's make sure Kuato--

869
01:21:52,816 --> 01:21:56,778
Wake up! Wake up!
Come on, wake up!

870
01:21:58,112 --> 01:22:00,699
They found us! Shit!
Let's go!

871
01:22:01,907 --> 01:22:04,160
Wake up! Snap out of it!
Come on!

872
01:22:08,747 --> 01:22:10,123
They found us!

873
01:22:10,207 --> 01:22:11,708
- Everybody out!
- Melina!

874
01:22:11,792 --> 01:22:13,877
Get moving! Get out!

875
01:22:15,127 --> 01:22:15,878
Get out!

876
01:22:25,805 --> 01:22:27,889
Everybody out! Get out!

877
01:22:33,562 --> 01:22:36,021
Get to the air lock! Follow me!

878
01:22:37,648 --> 01:22:39,275
Benny, come on!

879
01:22:43,319 --> 01:22:45,949
- Benny!
- I'm coming!

880
01:23:05,090 --> 01:23:08,719
Put these spacesuits on!
We're going outside!

881
01:23:11,638 --> 01:23:13,388
Benny, hurry.

882
01:23:20,854 --> 01:23:22,814
Congratulations, Quaid.

883
01:23:22,856 --> 01:23:25,150
You led us right to him.

884
01:23:25,233 --> 01:23:27,986
How can you do this?
You're a mutant.

885
01:23:28,945 --> 01:23:30,864
I got four kids to feed.

886
01:23:30,947 --> 01:23:33,115
So what happened to number five?

887
01:23:35,576 --> 01:23:38,204
Shit, man. You got me.

888
01:23:38,288 --> 01:23:39,996
I ain't even married.

889
01:23:40,038 --> 01:23:42,206
Now put your fucking hands
in the air!

890
01:23:48,086 --> 01:23:49,547
Quaid.

891
01:23:51,631 --> 01:23:53,675
Quaid.

892
01:23:55,385 --> 01:23:59,680
Forget it, man.
His fortunetelling days are over.

893
01:24:01,432 --> 01:24:04,311
Start the reactor.

894
01:24:04,394 --> 01:24:06,269
Free Mars.

895
01:24:11,399 --> 01:24:13,986
Mr. Cohaagen
would like to talk to you.

896
01:24:21,826 --> 01:24:24,202
So this is the great man.

897
01:24:29,166 --> 01:24:31,208
No wonder he kept out of sight.

898
01:24:33,462 --> 01:24:35,422
Well, my boy...

899
01:24:37,631 --> 01:24:38,716
you're a hero.

900
01:24:38,800 --> 01:24:39,884
Fuck you.

901
01:24:39,967 --> 01:24:43,720
Don't be modest.
Kuato is dead.

902
01:24:43,762 --> 01:24:48,099
The resistance is completely wiped out,
and you were the key to the whole thing.

903
01:24:48,183 --> 01:24:49,602
He's lying.

904
01:24:50,476 --> 01:24:52,645
You two-faced bastard.

905
01:24:54,523 --> 01:24:58,192
You can't blame him, angel.
He's innocent.

906
01:24:59,819 --> 01:25:04,239
You see, Quaid, none of my people
could get close to Kuato.

907
01:25:04,322 --> 01:25:07,242
Fucking mutants
could always sniff us out.

908
01:25:07,325 --> 01:25:11,411
So Hauser and I sat down
and invented you, the perfect mole.

909
01:25:11,495 --> 01:25:14,666
You know you're lying.
Hauser turned against you.

910
01:25:18,460 --> 01:25:20,421
That's what we wanted
you to think.

911
01:25:20,505 --> 01:25:24,632
The fact is, Hauser volunteered
to become Doug Quaid.

912
01:25:24,715 --> 01:25:27,719
It was the only way
to fool the psychics.

913
01:25:27,803 --> 01:25:29,302
Get your story straight.

914
01:25:29,386 --> 01:25:32,890
This idiot has been trying to kill me
ever since I went to Rekall.

915
01:25:32,974 --> 01:25:35,268
You don't kill somebody
you're trying to plant.

916
01:25:35,309 --> 01:25:39,272
He wasn't in on it.
You set him off by going to Rekall.

917
01:25:39,313 --> 01:25:42,273
- So why am I still alive?
- We gave you lots of help.

918
01:25:42,314 --> 01:25:44,276
- Benny here.
- My pleasure, man.

919
01:25:44,317 --> 01:25:47,904
The guy with the suitcase,
the mask, the money...

920
01:25:47,946 --> 01:25:51,907
the message from Hauser,
all of that was set up by us.

921
01:25:51,991 --> 01:25:54,493
Sorry. Too perfect.

922
01:25:54,577 --> 01:25:56,244
Perfect, my ass!

923
01:25:56,286 --> 01:25:58,914
You pop your memory cap
before we can activate you.

924
01:25:58,998 --> 01:26:03,084
Richter goes hog-wild, screwing up
everything I spent a year planning.

925
01:26:03,168 --> 01:26:06,004
Frankly, I'm amazed it worked.

926
01:26:07,173 --> 01:26:08,630
Well, Cohaagen...

927
01:26:08,672 --> 01:26:12,342
I have to hand it to you.
It's the best mind-fuck yet.

928
01:26:13,511 --> 01:26:16,804
Well, don't take my word for it.

929
01:26:17,972 --> 01:26:21,100
- Someone you trust wants to talk to you.
- Who is it this time?

930
01:26:21,142 --> 01:26:23,144
My mother?

931
01:26:25,189 --> 01:26:26,648
Howdy, Quaid.

932
01:26:26,690 --> 01:26:30,191
If you're listening to this,
it means that Kuato is dead...

933
01:26:30,275 --> 01:26:32,653
and you have led us to him.

934
01:26:32,695 --> 01:26:34,695
I knew you wouldn't let me down.

935
01:26:34,778 --> 01:26:36,948
Sorry for the shit
I've put you through, but hey...

936
01:26:37,032 --> 01:26:39,534
what are friends for?

937
01:26:39,618 --> 01:26:42,913
I would like to wish you happiness
and long life, old buddy...

938
01:26:42,996 --> 01:26:45,999
but unfortunately,
this is not gonna happen.

939
01:26:46,041 --> 01:26:50,211
You see, it's my body you've got there
and I want it back.

940
01:26:50,294 --> 01:26:54,546
Sorry to be an lndian giver,
but I was here first.

941
01:26:54,630 --> 01:26:57,216
So adios, amigo.

942
01:26:57,300 --> 01:27:00,509
And thanks for not
getting yourself killed.

943
01:27:00,593 --> 01:27:03,223
Hey, maybe we'll meet
in our dreams.

944
01:27:06,850 --> 01:27:08,769
You never know.

945
01:27:13,522 --> 01:27:15,608
You bastards!

946
01:27:33,749 --> 01:27:35,251
Let go of me!

947
01:27:51,266 --> 01:27:53,433
- Ready?
- Auto.

948
01:27:53,517 --> 01:27:56,437
- Check.
- Ready to go, sir.

949
01:27:58,437 --> 01:28:00,691
Relax, Quaid.

950
01:28:00,732 --> 01:28:04,111
- You'll like being Hauser.
- The guy's a fucking asshole.

951
01:28:04,194 --> 01:28:07,446
That's not true.
He's one of my best friends.

952
01:28:07,530 --> 01:28:10,450
Besides, he's got
a big house and a Mercedes.

953
01:28:10,534 --> 01:28:14,537
And you like Melina, right?
You'll get to fuck her every night.

954
01:28:14,620 --> 01:28:17,746
That's right.
She's going to be Hauser's babe.

955
01:28:17,788 --> 01:28:20,000
I'll bust his balls.

956
01:28:22,127 --> 01:28:24,420
Uh-uh, princess.

957
01:28:24,503 --> 01:28:26,922
We're having you fixed.

958
01:28:26,964 --> 01:28:30,344
You're going to be respectful,
compliant...

959
01:28:30,428 --> 01:28:33,929
and appreciative,
the way a woman should be.

960
01:28:37,682 --> 01:28:39,767
Mr. Cohaagen, telephone.

961
01:28:42,521 --> 01:28:44,187
Yes? What is it?

962
01:28:44,271 --> 01:28:47,107
The oxygen level
is bottoming out in Sector G.

963
01:28:47,149 --> 01:28:49,360
What do you want me
to do about it?

964
01:28:49,444 --> 01:28:53,488
- Don't do anything.
- But they won't last an hour, sir.

965
01:28:53,572 --> 01:28:54,657
Fuck 'em.

966
01:28:54,741 --> 01:28:57,283
It'll be a good lesson
to the others.

967
01:28:57,366 --> 01:29:00,078
You got what you want.
Give these people air.

968
01:29:00,120 --> 01:29:03,913
My friend, in five minutes
you won't give a shit about the people.

969
01:29:03,955 --> 01:29:05,248
Fire it up, Doc.

970
01:29:05,332 --> 01:29:07,418
Excuse me, Doctor.

971
01:29:07,501 --> 01:29:09,668
- Is he gonna remember any of this?
- Not a thing.

972
01:29:10,586 --> 01:29:11,837
Oh, really?

973
01:29:22,307 --> 01:29:23,974
Quaid, I'm having a party tonight.

974
01:29:24,016 --> 01:29:26,769
Why don't you and Melina drop by.
Remind him, Doc.

975
01:29:26,852 --> 01:29:29,186
- Sure.
- See you at the party.

976
01:29:43,742 --> 01:29:46,244
Keep still.
Fighting just makes it hurt.

977
01:29:59,048 --> 01:30:01,841
If you don't keep still,
you'll end up psychotic.

978
01:30:06,013 --> 01:30:07,473
Hey, don't!

979
01:30:14,435 --> 01:30:16,145
Melina, hold on!

980
01:30:39,042 --> 01:30:42,379
Are you all right?
Are you still you?

981
01:30:42,421 --> 01:30:45,841
I'm not sure, dear.
What do you think?

982
01:30:48,676 --> 01:30:50,094
Let's get the hell out of here.

983
01:31:17,619 --> 01:31:19,953
You have to make a decision, sir.

984
01:31:30,423 --> 01:31:31,674
Kill him.

985
01:31:32,882 --> 01:31:34,884
It's about goddamn time.

986
01:32:27,139 --> 01:32:29,936
- Where are you going?
- To the reactor.

987
01:32:30,019 --> 01:32:33,771
- What reactor?
- The one in the mines. Come on!

988
01:32:33,854 --> 01:32:37,815
People are dying, Quaid!
Stop! We've got to get air!

989
01:32:37,857 --> 01:32:41,070
The reactor makes air.
That's Cohaagen's secret. Let's go.

990
01:32:41,153 --> 01:32:42,738
Where's this reactor come from?

991
01:32:42,821 --> 01:32:44,863
- Aliens built it.
- Aliens?

992
01:32:44,947 --> 01:32:48,284
- Are you sure about this?
- It's just up ahead.

993
01:32:50,869 --> 01:32:52,120
What the hell--

994
01:33:16,601 --> 01:33:17,560
Quaid!

995
01:33:17,602 --> 01:33:20,730
Hey, Quaid, you remember me?

996
01:33:20,814 --> 01:33:23,148
Benny! Benny's the name!

997
01:33:37,287 --> 01:33:38,788
Oh, that's good!

998
01:33:44,584 --> 01:33:46,879
I'm gonna drill you, sucker!

999
01:33:46,921 --> 01:33:48,879
I'm gonna grind you up!

1000
01:33:55,928 --> 01:33:57,930
I'm coming!

1001
01:33:58,015 --> 01:33:59,683
I'm coming for you, baby!

1002
01:34:15,153 --> 01:34:17,407
What the fuck is this?

1003
01:34:23,954 --> 01:34:26,081
Damn this piece of Martian junk!

1004
01:34:28,458 --> 01:34:31,210
Hey, Quaid,
I'm gonna squash you!

1005
01:34:32,170 --> 01:34:34,087
Benny, here!

1006
01:34:37,258 --> 01:34:38,885
Where the fuck are you?

1007
01:34:44,556 --> 01:34:46,309
Screw you!

1008
01:34:52,356 --> 01:34:54,439
Quaid, get over here!

1009
01:34:54,522 --> 01:34:56,274
What is it?

1010
01:34:57,233 --> 01:34:58,319
There's an opening.

1011
01:34:59,446 --> 01:35:01,112
I knew it.

1012
01:35:29,847 --> 01:35:33,140
This whole thing is one big reactor
made out of terbinium.

1013
01:35:33,224 --> 01:35:36,645
Cohaagen knows it makes air.
The bastard won't turn it on.

1014
01:35:36,686 --> 01:35:37,979
Of course not.

1015
01:35:38,021 --> 01:35:40,981
If Mars had an atmosphere,
he'd lose control.

1016
01:35:42,150 --> 01:35:43,568
See down there?

1017
01:35:44,694 --> 01:35:47,154
It's a glacier.

1018
01:35:47,196 --> 01:35:50,324
The whole core of Mars is ice.

1019
01:35:50,366 --> 01:35:52,784
The reactor melts it...

1020
01:35:52,867 --> 01:35:54,702
and it releases the oxygen.

1021
01:35:54,786 --> 01:35:56,162
Come on.

1022
01:35:56,204 --> 01:35:59,206
- Enough for everyone to breathe?
- Sure.

1023
01:35:59,289 --> 01:36:02,209
Enough for the whole planet.

1024
01:36:02,292 --> 01:36:04,547
If we turn it on in time.

1025
01:36:11,177 --> 01:36:13,136
Come on. Come on!

1026
01:36:30,319 --> 01:36:31,402
Hold on.

1027
01:37:02,639 --> 01:37:03,598
Now!

1028
01:37:34,127 --> 01:37:35,337
Son of a bitch.

1029
01:37:43,050 --> 01:37:43,717
Go!

1030
01:37:47,472 --> 01:37:49,639
He's got a hologram!

1031
01:38:11,493 --> 01:38:14,163
You think this is
the real Quaid? It is.

1032
01:39:34,026 --> 01:39:36,153
You're coming with me!

1033
01:39:49,624 --> 01:39:51,875
See you at the party, Richter.

1034
01:40:30,119 --> 01:40:31,369
Don't touch that!

1035
01:40:31,411 --> 01:40:33,413
Get away! Get back!

1036
01:40:33,455 --> 01:40:34,915
What are you afraid of?

1037
01:40:34,956 --> 01:40:37,375
- Turn it on.
- Impossible!

1038
01:40:37,458 --> 01:40:40,586
Once the reaction starts, it'll spread
to all the terbinium in the planet.

1039
01:40:40,670 --> 01:40:42,964
Mars will go into
global meltdown.

1040
01:40:43,047 --> 01:40:45,716
That's why the aliens
never turned it on.

1041
01:40:45,800 --> 01:40:47,885
And you expect me
to believe you?

1042
01:40:47,968 --> 01:40:52,514
Who gives a shit what you believe?
ln 30 seconds you'll be dead.

1043
01:40:52,597 --> 01:40:55,977
Then I'll blow this place up
and be home in time for corn flakes.

1044
01:40:59,561 --> 01:41:01,481
I didn't want it to end this way.

1045
01:41:01,564 --> 01:41:03,606
I wanted Hauser back.
But no.

1046
01:41:04,816 --> 01:41:07,069
You had to be Quaid!

1047
01:41:07,111 --> 01:41:09,572
- I am Quaid.
- You're nothing!

1048
01:41:09,656 --> 01:41:12,740
You're nobody!
You're a stupid dream.

1049
01:41:12,824 --> 01:41:16,827
Well, all dreams come to an end.

1050
01:42:31,604 --> 01:42:33,982
Melina, hold on!

1051
01:42:34,024 --> 01:42:35,648
Don't do it!

1052
01:42:35,732 --> 01:42:37,693
We'll all die!

1053
01:42:38,569 --> 01:42:41,028
Everybody will die!

1054
01:43:44,087 --> 01:43:45,628
Quaid!

1055
01:49:00,705 --> 01:49:03,126
I can't believe it.
It's like a dream.

1056
01:49:04,376 --> 01:49:06,044
What's wrong?

1057
01:49:06,128 --> 01:49:09,921
I just had a terrible thought.
What if this is a dream?

1058
01:49:11,424 --> 01:49:14,510
Well, then kiss me quick
before you wake up.